\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Two-tier diagnostic hierarchy (Qwen-7B). Tier~1 signals (exceptions, assertion outcomes) are each individually near-perfect and sufficient. Tier~2 (loop summaries) carries moderate signal but is fully subsumed. Combining tiers introduces noise: exception-only (99.83\%) $>$ VOTA (99.41\%), $p$=0.01.}}{5}{table.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:hierarchy}{{3}{5}{Two-tier diagnostic hierarchy (Qwen-7B). Tier~1 signals (exceptions, assertion outcomes) are each individually near-perfect and sufficient. Tier~2 (loop summaries) carries moderate signal but is fully subsumed. Combining tiers introduces noise: exception-only (99.83\%) $>$ VOTA (99.41\%), $p$=0.01}{table.caption.7}{}}
